   "id": 3513916,
   "postDate": "2026-08-18T00:05:14.913Z",
   "rawMarkdown": "Really happy 😄 to see Kaggle competitions becoming more and more popular, with so many new teams joining.\n\nFor comparison:\n\n* **RSNA 2025:** finished with **1,149 teams**\n* **RSNA 2026:** only **12 days in**, and we already have **1,832 teams**\n\nThe leaderboard is also moving incredibly fast. The current **#1 public LB is already around 0.951**, while publicly shared solutions are already reaching around **0.92**.\n\nSo I’m curious: **where do you think the final ceiling will be?**\n\nIf BirdCLEF+ 2026 is any indication of how much solutions can improve during a competition, could we eventually see something like:\n\n* **#1 final/Public LB:** ~**0.97**\n* **Best publicly shared solution:** ~**0.95**\n\nOf course, medical imaging competitions can behave very differently, and CV/generalization on the private set may change the picture a lot.\n\nBut with this many strong teams joining this early, one thing seems certain: **this is going to be a really tough competition. 😄**\n\nCurious what others think the end-game scores might look like.\n",
   "content": "<p>Really happy 😄 to see Kaggle competitions becoming more and more popular, with so many new teams joining.</p>\n<p>For comparison:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>RSNA 2025:</strong> finished with <strong>1,149 teams</strong></li>\n<li><strong>RSNA 2026:</strong> only <strong>12 days in</strong>, and we already have <strong>1,832 teams</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>The leaderboard is also moving incredibly fast. The current <strong>#1 public LB is already around 0.951</strong>, while publicly shared solutions are already reaching around <strong>0.92</strong>.</p>\n<p>So I’m curious: <strong>where do you think the final ceiling will be?</strong></p>\n<p>If BirdCLEF+ 2026 is any indication of how much solutions can improve during a competition, could we eventually see something like:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>#1 final/Public LB:</strong> ~<strong>0.97</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Best publicly shared solution:</strong> ~<strong>0.95</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Of course, medical imaging competitions can behave very differently, and CV/generalization on the private set may change the picture a lot.</p>\n<p>But with this many strong teams joining this early, one thing seems certain: <strong>this is going to be a really tough competition. 😄</strong></p>\n<p>Curious what others think the end-game scores might look like.</p>",
   "parent": {},
